Anti-unrest police officers intervened immediately and without regard.
The police have announced that 600 to 700 people, according to your assessment mainly members of "the Blacks Blocs", these extremely violent splinter groups, who have already made themselves famous at the Nato Summit in Strasbourg, were arrested in eastern France, in April.
The Climate Justice Action (CJA), one of the organizers of the demonstration (CJA), has sharply criticized the conditions under which hundreds of militant supporters had been arrested "without distinction," and has underlined that about a hundred of you were "still held in the streets on Saturday evening," despite the extreme cold handcuffs and into seating.
The rather peaceful move has gone from parliament towards the Bella Center, where the negotiations took place.
The protesters stopped about 500 yards from the building without trying to get inside.
