Endesa and Barcelona by electric car
Together with the city of Barcelona, the power company Endesa has created the "LIVE office".
This is a project for the development and promotion of electric cars in the Catalan capital.
The "LIVE office" (logistics for the introduction of the electric car) will define and coordinate the roadmap for the introduction of the electric car in the city and make agreements regarding mobility through administration, coordination, subsidization, etc.
On the other hand, the MOVELE project is being developed for the promotion of the electric car and summarizing opinions and measures of the areas involved.
This is an attempt to advance the means of transport of the future.
3 "Electric cities"
However, Barcelona isn’t the only city to be involved in the introduction of the electric car in Spain.
Madrid and Seville are also taking part in this project.
These are the three government-chosen cities in the MOVELE project to accelerate the introduction of the electric car.
The electricity company Endesa has already signed a framework agreement with the government of Catalonia (la Generalitat).
This framework agreement seeks to promote the activities of research and technological development in the Autonomous Community of Catalonia.
These activities involve, among other things, such activities associated with energy and, in particular, their performance.
However, it is by no means the only initiative that Endesa participates in order to the promotion of electric cars.
The company participates in standardization groups throughout Europe and maintains a number of additional projects such as G4V, ELVIRE or CENIT VERDE.
Zapatero sees 'a horizon of calm' for the automotive sector
The government president, José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero, prophesies "a horizon of calm" to the Spanish automotive industry, which is the country's greatest exporter.
At the presentation of the economic report for 2009 by the President of the Government, Zapatero once again recalled the measures that the government launched in support of the automotive sector in the course of the financial year.
"Without the plan for the competitiveness of the car industry today, we would have a panorama of neglect and closure of some of our main production plants today," he said.
"Thanks to this plan and the willingness of car manufacturers to continue producing in Spain in a highly competitive industry in the future, we can see a calm horizon for the future of this industry, which is our largest export industry," he added.
He also recalled that the Competitiveness plan, which is part of the overall plan for the automotive industry (PIA), provided €800 million for projects by 19 vehicle manufacturers and 137 suppliers, which in turn accounted for more than €3 billion.
The head of government stated that these investments are intended both for the development of new models and for the modernisation of existing products and processes.
Zapatero also underlined the government's measures to stimulate demand, in reference to Plan 2000E, applied in cooperation with the Autonomous Communities and car manufacturers.
According to the head of government, this plan allows the exhaust gases of new vehicles sold on the Spanish market to be reduced on average by 6%, which in turn led to a "strong increase" in registrations, which increased "by 40 percent" in November.
On 20,000 square meters of classic vehicles
In Madrid, the first edition of the International Classic Automobile Fair will be held, an exhibition for professionals and lovers of the world of engines.
This fair will take place from 5 to 7 February 2010 at the Pabellón de Cristal of the Casa de Campo in Madrid.
On an exhibition area of 20,000 square meters 200 domestic and foreign exhibitors will demonstrate their brands.
Not only can you admire classic motorcycles and vehicles, but you’ll alsove you’ll find all imaginable items in connection with the world of engines at ClassicAuto Madrid.
In this way you can find accessories, spare parts, components, fabric accessories, accessories, publications, miniature cars, etc. from the exhibitors at the trade fair.
Hundreds of items from the world of classic engines that will delight collectors and lovers.
Among the companies that will participate in this fair include Clásicos de Mos and Good Old Times, vehicle sales; Juan Lumbreras, restorations; Coupe-Francisco Pueche, sales and restoration of automobiles, specializing in Mercedes Benz.
Skill tests in the outdoor area
In addition, the sales activities at this trade fair are complemented by parallel events: meetings, sports vehicle exhibitions, skill tests, events and competitions.
Skill tests with classic cars and motorcycles are also carried out on a specially set-up race track in the outdoor area of the exhibition grounds.
Mazda3 i-Stop: Eco-friendly sportsmanship
Mazda wants to prove that sportsmanship is quite compatible with the protection of the environment.
For this reason, Mazda recently introduced the automatic stop and start-up system of the engine, baptized in the name i-Stop, a device that is currently only available for the 2.0 petrol engine with 150 hp.
This second generation of Mazdas 3 stands out for its good grades in the overall picture.
The final processing, the execution of the vehicle, the comfort, its road behavior, the mechanics, the i-stop system ...
All these aspects are "very good" on the new Mazda3.
Beginning with the front seats, you can see that the front seats offer excellent ergonomics and good support.
Furthermore, the play of the steering wheel is excellent.
When looking at the unit, which consists of the instrument panel and the dashboard, it can be noted that Mazda with a variety of buttons and switches in the eye-catching colors red and blue, on the same line as the Japanese trend towards a futuristic interior design.
This style reminds us in part of the style of the Honda Civics.
Therefore, it can easily be said that both the Mazda 3 and the Civic, both Japanese models, stand out from the sobriety of German automobiles, especially the Volkswagen Golf, which everyone wants to surpass.
More than ever, the passenger compartment of these two Japanese compact cars offers the appropriate comfort so that four adults can drive extremely comfortably.
To all this comes a spacious and clearly shaped trunk.
Until now, the stop and start-up system is only available for the 2-liter petrol engine with 150 hp and a 6-speed transmission.
This engine is a real pleasure. It stands out for its fineness due to its quiet noises, its performances and its low consumption.
And all those who don’t drive many kilometers a year should consider this i-Stop with gasoline engine because of its great comfort in gear shifting and its low consumption, even if at Mazda especially the diesel models are the best-selling.
With regard to the equipment, the so-called Sportive model selected for the test drive is a special feature, as it has a much larger number of elements from the standard equipment.
Above all, the assistant for lane change (RVM) stands out from the production equipment, which thereby eliminates the blind spot, but also the controls for traction and stability, cruise control, the light-sensitive interior mirror, the on-board computer with a large screen, the sensors for parking, independent air conditioning, rain and light sensors, Bluetooth and audio bluetooth, as well as the chrome-plated 17.
In addition, this version also includes, as if this were not enough of equipment, the Premium package, which contains the following for an additional 1,500 euros: in addition to other elements above all the learnable Bixenon headlights and the sound system BOSE with CD loader.
Conclusion
The Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the best compact cars in its class.
It is particularly outstanding in terms of the materials used, because of its handling and the variety of equipment.
In addition, those who do not travel many kilometers a year can also buy the i-stop version, which is only available with a 2.0 petrol engine with 150 hp.
The only negative thing about this model is its somewhat high price, which ranges between 21,770 euros for the model Luxury and 23,270 euros for the test-drived model Sportive.
In return at this high price, however, the Mazda3 offers us every day the highest driving pleasure.
