Manuel Vicent's poker game
Manuel Vicent presents in "Poker of the Aces" (Alfaguara, depictions of Fernando Vicente) to the thirty X-ray images of writers who have accompanied him in his literary life (and, in some cases, even in real life).
In doing so, he does not use a foreseeable and terrifying genre (short biography, life and work), but looks for a similarity to the glowing centrepiece of the creator.
The journey is exciting and Vicent spares neither horrors nor enlightenments.
Except that this book is a delicious reading pleasure, it is also a motivative invitation to read and read again and again.
Here are some excerpts from the book.
When reading his pages, I found out that the Mediterranean is not a sea, but rather a spiritual, almost sensual impulse, just as I have always felt, without finding words for it: the joy as opposed to ominous fate, morality without guilt and innocence without any God.
About Samuel Beckett: "Nihilist, allegorical Christian, he wrote about what he had in the blood, not in his mind, between impotencence and ignorancy, with a stunning poetic humour, without any sense, like the knife blade that almost killed him."
“Our husband was captivated by this woman with a passion that lasted for thirteen years, in such a way that the flesh the emotions due to adultery combined with the pleasure of remorse, a spiritual privilege that consisted in coming to heaven on the detour of perison.”
James Joyce: "The Odysseus" was published by Sylvia Beach in Paris in 1922. This is one of the 8000 peaks in the worldwide literature, you have to climb up the north face, on the wall, on which the best mountaineers try again and again."
William Faulkner: "He was a funny owl.
He sometimes said of himself that he was the heir to a landowner of the county and again other times he said he was the son of a black and a crocodile.
Both dreams testified to a certain greatness.”
About Louis-Ferdinand Céline: This writer picked up the insane cry that was shouted out by that personality from Munich, so that his echo echoed in his literary way until deep into the night of the 20th century. He did this on a journey on which he fled from himself and begged posterity with a speech full of violence before the worms.
About Dorothy Parker: "One day she knelt and prayed: my venerable God, I ask you to do everything in your power so that I finally stop writing like a woman."
About Joseph Conrad: "On his tomb these verses of Spencer are engraved: ′sleep after the effort,/ after the thunderstorm of the harbor, / the rest after the war, / after a full life you find pleasure in death."
About Virginia Wolf: "In her luggage she always had her depression with her.
The husband took it with complete normality when she told him that Edward VII spied on them between the azales or sang the birds in Greek.
Not a single other case is known, where the man had so much patience and was in love with a neurotic whose literary talent was still much greater than her madness.”
Pío Baroja: "What else did Martín-Santos do but try to instigate Joyce into Baroja?
What did Benet mean if he didn't introduce Baroja to Faulkner's weapons?
What did Cela do besides destroy that man's glory so that he could put himself on this pedestal?"
Cowardly aggression
My 70-year-old mother was walking through our district in the village of Fuenlabrada last week, when suddenly a group of young people between the ages of 15 and 18 walked next to her and our dog, our dog is a mongrel, whom we brought from the shelter and who weighs just six kilos, and then out of the skay they gave him two footsteps and injured him severely.
Our indignation cannot even be put into words, since it is incomprehensible to us where the fun should be in a cheap aggression against a small and helpless animal, which was of course carried out on a leash.
In addition, there was the suffocatiation that a woman who was walking leisurely when she wanted to rebuke these people because of the incident, she even feared for her own life, because if such a madman attacks a dog, he will perhaps also do the same with a woman, a child, an elderly gentleman or probably even with anyone who is weaker than himself.
The incident happened in a normally quiet neighbourhood at five in the afternoon on an ordinary Tuesday.
The dog has been crying all day.
Of course, we filed a complaint in a nearby police department, but we have great doubts as to whether this will bring anything at all and to prevent any prejudices from the very beginning, we only want to make it clear that the cowardly criminals were Spaniards.
Our indignation at what has happened has prompted us to report this incident.
We can't understand what's going on in the minds of these young people, that they find a cheap attack on a helpless animal funny, on an animal that gives us love, society and friendship.
We don't know where the good education and respect for the animals and persons have remained.
Michelin and Fesvial together to use the helmet
Tire manufacturer Michelin, in cooperation with the Spanish Foundation for Road Safety (Fesvial), has launched a campaign to promote helmet use, especially among younger motorcyclists.
This initiative thus seeks to draw attention to the importance of helmet use, since this is ultimately the only protective element that can prevent head injuries or even death in the event of a motorcycle accident.
Michelin pointed out that this campaign is part of its commitment in terms of road safety, which includes "far more than just designing and manufacturing products that are becoming increasingly safe with each passing day" and further reaffirmed that, even with other actions of educational and informative character, they contribute to getting one step closer to this goal every day.
This new campaign to promote helmet use on the motorcycle, which runs under the slogan 'To be or not to be', will distribute posters to over 500 motorcycle workshops in a first phase in order to achieve the best possible distribution.
To conclude, Michelin emphasized that road safety is "a constant concern" of the company, and precisely because, as a manufacturer of tires for two-wheeled vehicles, they are always committed to ensuring that one of its main goals must be the development of ever safer products.
The sale of small trucks rises again somewhat
After almost two years, the car market for vans finally begins to see some light at the end of the dark tunnel.
The 9,425 vehicles registered in Spain in November represent an increase of 12.6% in terms of 2008, and, more importantly, they are thus the first increase ever after 22 consecutive months with a steady decline, according to the figures presented by the manufacturers' association Anfac and the car dealer association Ganvam.
However, these good figures can only be enjoyed with great caution at the moment, since the reference data used for the comparison of November 2008 are, which was a particularly poor sales year with a 60% decrease in the previous year.
However, it must be borne in mind that, apart from the increase in the last month, the total approvals of these 11 months are still 40% below the sales figures for the previous financial year.
Since January, a total of 95,853 vehicles have been solded, but in this number all vehicles that make up the van market are included: descendants of passenger cars, pick-ups, vans, small vans and lighter small trucks/chassis.
Furthermore, there are still the same storm clouds in the sky, which most affect the demand, because even if some of the vehicles are bought by private individuals, the majority of sales to small and medium-sized enterprises, which in almost 100% of all cases make the purchase with a third-party financing.
Thus, to these restrictions, which are the consequence of the turned-down money tap of the credit institutions, one must include other factors, such as the increase in the unemployment rate or the continuation of the bad economic situation.
With this panorama and in contrast to passenger cars, the financial support in the purchase of a vehicle of plan 2000E has helped little.
However, this plan is not only intended for private individuals, the self-employed and small companies also have the right if they want to buy a van up to 3.5 tons with a CO2 ejection, which must not exceed 160 grams per kilometre, but the low sales figures speak for themselves.
Just yesterday, Ganvam had reminded that it is absolutely necessary on the part of the state to pay special attention to these small trucks as well as, of course, the industrial vehicles (lorries and buses).
The car dealer association predicts a similar year for 2010 to the just past, for which it expects a loss of sales (for passenger cars and SUVs) of 19%.
Support for braking manoeuvres in critical situations is now mandatory
As was already the case at that time with the anti-lock braking braking system ABS and what is happening right now with stability control ESP, the auxiliary systems for braking in emergencies must become a mandatory equipment in European cars.
In fact, they are already mandatory for all newly registered passenger cars and light vans, for the remaining vehicles a waiting period until the end of February 2011 has been set.
The aim of the European Union is to improve the protection of pedestrians, but these braking systems can also help to prevent many rear-end collisions due to their functioning.
The task of the emergency braking assistant is to exert more pressure on the brakes in the event of a critical braking manoeuvre, which the system recognizes on the brake pedal on the basis of the braking strength executed by the driver.
However, this system does not exert this pressure until the end.
According to an investigation commissioned by the component manufacturer for the Bosch vehicles, one-third of the drivers involved in an accident no longer even came to stepping on the brake pedal before the collision and half of them had not braked with full force.
Up to 1,100 accidents
The braking aid, on the other hand, engages the braking system with maximum force and thereby reduces the braking time and thus also the braking distance that a car travels during the braking process.
According to a study by the EU, up to 1,100 fatal accidents in which pedestrians are harmed could be prevented every year if all cars were equipped with this type of emergency braking assistant.
There would be even fewer accidents - it is expected that one in four accidents could be prevented with personal injury - as soon as the so-called intelligent emergency braking systems become popular.
Then the vehicle is equipped with a system that detects obstacles (via radar or a camera) and warns the driver, at the same time already exerting slight pressure on the brakes.
If the driver responds, the system helps him to increase the pressure on the brake pedal if necessary.
If the driver does not respond to the warning and even if the collision is unavoidable, the brake assistant exerts the maximum pressure on the brakes in order to keep the damage as low as possible.
General Motors postpones plan for Opel until January
While the staff of the Opel plant in Figueruelas (Zaragoza) have already been informed by Nick Reilly, the new chairman of General Motors (GM) Europe, that production of the new Meriva will start in the first week of April, probably on the 8th, according to Javier Ortega, the American vehicle maker points out that it needs more time to finalize the rescue plan for Opel.
Nick Reilly, the new chairman of GM Europa, wants to ensure that the side concerned gives its approval in advance to every single point of the plan.
And for this reason, it may be that the final document, presented first to the workers and then to the governments of the countries in which there are works, will be postponed until the beginning of 2010.
On the other hand, GM is assured that it will make a decision regarding the sale of Saab in the next few days.
It’s not surprising that the Swedish government has increased the pressure on the American carmaker to make a decision as soon as possible.
GM admits to being in contact with some potential new buyers.
One of these buyers could be Geely, who would also like to buy Volvo, but the option of the Dutch manufacturer of Skyper sports cars, which is backed by the Russian group Converg is gaininginging.
If none of these buyers come to an agreement, GM could sell some assets to China's BAIC.
The decision to conclude Saab at the end of the year if it has not been solded by then will continue.
At the wheel of Porsche Boxster Spyder
For the development of their latest and very expensive jewel, the engineers used Boxster S as the basis and really managed to make it 80 kilos lighter, with which it now weighs only 1,275 kilos.
In order to create something like this, they first dispensed with the automatic folding roof, which was replaced by a tent wall roof with manual propulsion, so that only 21 kilos have been saved; thanks to the aluminum doors used in this model "disappeare" another 15; by the removal of the air conditioning again 13; in addition, the fuel tank has been reduced from 64 to 54 liters.
Then, by omitting the CDR-30 audio system, they had again reached six kilos less and by replacing the door handles made of fabric the missing kilo.
Although it is also available with the PDK dual-clutch transmission, the test drive was carried out with a vehicle with 6-speed manual transmissions, mainly on the smaller country roads of California, on mountain routes that were really very winding.
With his driving behavior you can only give him the note impeccably.
However, the reduction of his weight did not mean that he would no longer be so safe on the road.
It’s rather the opposite: for a long time we haven’t tested such a small and light model, which at the same time also gives you a feeling of great safety in the curves, even at high speed.
He is a small athlete, able to make his muscles warm during a low gear in the necessary time, until we give him the orders to race, to brake, to recover and then to get everything out of his engine again ...
He does everything he's been told. The car does everything that we suggest to him with our hands on the steering wheel, thanks to his steering, which is just as communicative as it is precise.
And he's doing it with a surgeon's precision.
An engine sound for all flavors
The sound of his V6 boxer with 320 hp (10 more than Boxster S) is extremely successful and you can increase it with the 'sport' option as well as by means of a system that can change the engine noise, which has already been used for the first time in the Panamera.
Accelerating ability is unimaginably brutal, regardless of whether it’s standing out of standing or when accelerating again.
The suspensions are strong, but not hard or uncomfortable.
The tarm on the country roads on which we drove with the Boxster Spyder was already quite damaged, but the car mastered the potholes well.
The electronic assistants had almost nothing to do at all on the entire track, even though at some of these curves we found ice at the dawn and roll split in the morning.
In summary, you can say that it is an ultra-light car, a car with which you have an indescribable pass, as it usually rarely exists and there is much more in it than just a small improvement of the Boxster Ss.
The car will be launched in February 2010 and will cost €70,831.
Bag girl'
The singer, a bosom friend of Karl Lagerfeld, is the face of the Coco Coco Cocoon cosmetic line and a casual starlet at the 'maison' fashion shows, she presents her evil face with the same neck rigidity as Chanel's pockets.
Much more than "Bad Girl," she's a "Bag Girl."
Baskonia gives itself a victory in Israel
The Caja Laboral, despite the many unusual players in Dusko Ivanovic's squad, celebrated an excellent triumph with 82-91 on his visit to the intricate football field of Maccabi Electra and thus comes in first place within his group after the great performance of Mirza Teletovic, who was the best of his team with eight triples (29 in the rating).
The team from Vitoria was able to replace the significant failures of Herrmann, Oleson, Huertas or Micov with a large dose of effort and teamwork, even if they had to wait for their victory until the bitter end.
The great hits from the perimeter with 16 rated triples contributed significantly to their final victory.
The game began with leading the blue-reds, who from the start put themselves at the top on the scoreboard.
Since the first four baskets of the team from Vitoria already came out of the perimeter, it could already be guessed that they had come onto the pitch with well-warmed wrists.
It was English and Teletovic who were mainly responsible for the 18-20 at the end of the first quarter.
The second quarter was hardly different, only that the team from Álava opted for an inner-sided game by Barac and for the game of Eliyahu, who on his return to the squad was received with whistles and applause, which is his home, to expand their advantage further until the break (34-43).
Teletovic was already beginning to stand out as the best of his squad with 13 points, even if the "minus six" rating from Splitter already suggested that this would not be the Brazilian's best evening.
Nevertheless, despite the clear advantage at the break, the game was far from decided and the Maccabeans wanted to remind the Vitorians once again that not everyone wins on their pitch, and thanks to the repeatedly attacking "Hand of Elías" they came back into the game.
Eidson and Pnini contributed decisively to the "yellows" turning the helm (50-49).
Even more Disadvantages
Ivanovic's team, injured but anything but dead, had to prepare a few moves with accuracy to get some air again and at one of them suddenly came Mirza Teletovic's pistol, who with three almost consecutive triples and with the support of English and Ribas ensured that on the scoreboard again soothing distance of (54-67) could be displayed, which the hoster at the end of the third quarter.
The Alavese were exposed in the last quarter and English and San Emeterio (60-75) already announced that they wouldn't allow anyone to take away from them the victory they honestly deserved in the first threes.
Nevertheless Pnini and Eidson, the best of their squad did not resign their squad and tried to give their squad again through three points off the line (70-77).
Nevertheless, and even though Splitter was put off the pitch because of foul, Ivanovic's team did not give up, defended well and although the Israelis were still catching up in the last minute (80-85), the game already had a winner and Tel Aviv lost for the first time this season.
Injuries prevented Unicaja from being the forehead
Unicaja loudly lost in Greece against Olympiacos and had to cede the lead in Group B of the Euroliga to him, in a game that was characterized by the failures on the part of the players of Unicajas (Freeland, Lima and Archibald), especially in the inside game, which facilitated victory for the Greeks.
The Málaga team was neither afraid of the mood in the Hall of Peace and Friendship nor of the opposing team, which is perhaps one of the strongest in Europe and has a lot of money.
Thanks to their offered game in first quarters, the Andalusians were allowed to start dreaming. An aggresive defense and three consecutive triples, two of them through Omar Cook and one through Guillem Rubio, dazzled the hosts with 12-18 in the 9th minute.
Olympiacos was surprised by the intensity of erein Unicaja, even if the domestic squad with an inside match between Bourousis, Vujcic and Schortsanitis managed that the scoreboard in the 13th minute 22-20 indicated in their favour, the minute in which there would almost have been the brawl between the two Americans Beverley and Williams due to an action and which is why both were disqualified.
The Greek team began to finally get warm and their superiority on both halves of the game, while the departure of Englishman Joel Freeland due to an injury and Carlos Jiménez's three self-induced mistakes left significant marks at the Unicaja.
Under their players in the inside field and the Lithuanian foreplayer Linas Kleizas, with his triples, they increased their advantage in the 19th minute to 44-32.
A catch-up was impossible
The third quarter was characterized by many attacks against Olympiaco's squad, which proved superior despite its 19 losses and even managed to make up for the difference of the 66-48 game played in Málaga in the 27th minute, which in turn caused the lead within the group to fluctuate.
Unicaja tried to override the many failures and the departure of Scot Robert Archibald, who was injured during the match.
Despite the many disadvantages for the Unicaja, some hope of 66-57 came again in the 31st minute thanks to the league and the triples of Cook and the use of Lewis.
Nevertheless, it was actually impossible, as soon as the Olympiacos attacked and showed his supremacy with centimeters within the basket area could not be braked.
The Croatian captain Nikola Vujcic managed in the 37th minute to raise the basket difference to 81-62 and Unicaja had to concede defeat and had to cede the lead to Olympiacos.
How much should you earn based on your profile in Facebook?
The users of Facebook can now, thanks to the new application Trovit, the search engine with the most ads of real estate, vacancies and cars in Spain, learn their salary that they should earn based on their profile.
The "How much should you earn?" calculates users' salaries based on more than 140,000 vacancies available at Trovit in Spain. Users have a form available in Facebook to enter their profession, professional experience , age and the city in which they work.
Already after a week after the application was available for the first time, the search engine found that the Spanish worker feels "poorly paid on average," Albert Ribera, said in a press release.
Spaniards are the worst-paid according to the data that Trovit possesses through its search engines in the UK and France.
A British programmer gets an annual gross salary of €45,226 and a Frenchman 31,059, as opposed to the €24,000 a Spaniard earns.
As a result, a truck driver has an annual net salary of €34,247 in England, €25,751 in France and €16,420 in Spain.
According to Trovit, the worst-paided job in Spain is that of a waiter with €11,592 net per year; followed by a seller's work with €14,725 and that of a worker with €15,667.
The most sought-after jobs on the internet in the past three months are those of a driver, half-day jobs and social workers.
Brazlia names Zelaya a date to leave
The Brazilian government has set a deadline for Manuel Zelaya's stay at its embassy in Tegucigalpa.
The president removed from office must leave the diplomatic mission by 27 January 2010 at the latest, when his mandate officially expires
Francisco Catunda, the trade delegate of the Brazilian embassy in the Honduran capital, confirmed to TV Globo that "Mel" knows he must have left the embassy in which he had found asylum since September 21.
"He's aware that he has to leave on January 27 because his mandate expires that day and he has to look for new accommodation."
The broadcaster also quoted the ex-president confirming his intention to leaving the embassy before the appointed date: "My point of view is to leave as soon as possible, logically with the backing of the government of Brazil," Zelaya explained over the phone.
After the November 29 elections (in which Porfirio Lobo emerged as the winner), Zelaya assured that he would stay at the Brazilian embassy until January.
However, he trieded to gain refuge in Brazil this week.
This, however, failed from Zelaya's refusal to acknowledge the status of an asylum-seeking politician, whom the "de facto" government, chaired by Roberto Micheletti, wanted to impose on him.
Thank you very much!
After the most tempting days since last sprend, inflation of assets was the predominant mood in the markets, uncertainty has returned again in the markets, which is by no means surprising, as this is its natural condition, in an environment in which brokers are making decisions about an inherently uncertain future.
The measure used to stabilise the markets was to settle the debt with the direct purchase of assets and to indirectly leave the liquidity free hand at interest rates moving around zero, so that in this way the banks buy assets for billing.
The central banks have already confirmed that the direct purchases of assets are virtually finished and, without questioning their heterodox policy on liquidity, are beginning to sprout some sand into the gear, as the BCE already did with its annual auction, which will take place next week.
This is why investors doubt the ability of the world economy to maintain the economic recovery without these heterodox measures and we are currently witnessing a reversal in reducing risk premiums.
The fugitivities of the exchanges and the differences in corporate bonuses are rising again, even if they are still far from the paranormal amounts they reached at the beginning of the year.
The states were forced to nationalize the private risks and the national debt rises again.
Quality is now relying on quality again and the USA, Japan and Germany are the preferred refuge of investors, which in turn leads to an increase in the differences between the countries of the eurozone with regard to Germany.
Until now, Spain has hardly been affected by this episode of instability, but then Standard & Poor's came along and threatened a new revision downwards regarding Spain's assessment.
On the other hand, there is no harm of some uncertainty to silence the defenders of the moral risk, who had once again tried to raise awareness among those responsible for world economic policy of what they had caused, since they had slowed down the devastating effects to which the restriction of loans led to the loss of jobs, when they should actually have decided a new day to give thanks.
Nevertheless, what happened in Dubai points to a tribal war between the Emirs in order to restore power in the Emirates and development in Greece has also been foreseen earlier.
A government that conceals the national debt, elections and a new government that is pulling on the same line.
Prodi made it in Italy to Berlusconi and Sócrates in Portugal to Durão Barroso.
It makes no sense that Ecofin save Hungary earlier this year from failing to meet its foreign payments and thus admits a eurozone member country to stop fulfilling its obligations.
On the other hand, it is logical that Ecofin has forced the Greek government to be transparent and to make its citizens obligatory in the need for exceptional measures in order to maintain the stability of state funds.
Yes, as expected, we are ahead of an episode of normalisation of risk premiums, after some debaucheries on excessive amounts, that would now be within what is expected.
In the case of Spain, you don't have to worry, as long as the differences in public debt increase at the same rate as Europe's corporate bonies.
However, if the European differences are reduced and the Spanish continues to increase, it would be a special Spanish risk.
Standard & Poor's is a farce. While the local early indicators are forcing much of market research institutes to prefer their scenarios for recovery and correcting their scenario upwards for 2011, including the OCDE and the European Commission, which once again come up with a Japanese scenario for the Spanish economy, all this does not promise a long lifespan despite warnings.
Once again, it seems that it is an excellent opportunity to buy Spanish shares, although at the moment "caution when driving" is required.
Connected branches
Iberdrola's chairman, Ignacio Sánchez Galán, was the first to appear before Parliament's sub-committee yesterday, where Spain's energy supplies are being debated these days.
After his appearance, which was followed by the chairman of Gas Natural-Fenosa, Rafael Villaseca, Galán gave the press some points about what he had submitted to the subcommittee behind closed doors.
According to Iberdrola's chairman, Spain will have to invest €50 billion and another €60 billion from that date by 2030, providing that the current nuclear power plants remain in operation.
If this is not the case, the required investments would not amount to 60 billion, but up to 95 billion.
However, Iberdrola is of the opinion that one should no longer invest in an increase in energy generation capacity, but in distribution networks and international networks.
From 2020, the question will change and one should increase performance.
His proposal focuses both on gas and coal plants with facilities to collect carbon dioxide and, of course, above all on renewable energies.
In this case, it assumes that 18,000 MW more is needed, under the prerequisition of course by other "support energies".
Galán, who believes that the bill for a sustainable economy that has just been passed by the government, is in line with what his company has demanded, by no means wanted to say anything against this law, such as creating incentives for national coal consumption, which would be exactly the opposite of all political strategies in the fight against climate change.
In his opinion, "in the long term, we are clearly focusing on this direction, in spite of a few "individual" measures, as the chairman of Iberdrola referred to.
Be it as it is, Galán thinks that one should already take the decisions on the investments, even if they are long-term, because it will take some time and a stable remuneration framework must be created in order to tackle them.
Ferrovial gets the 'handling' of Aer Lingus at ten airports
Ferrovial's subsidiary for services at on-the-ground airports, Swissport, is the preferred partner of the Irrelandic airline Aer Lingus for luggage service at ten European airports where they are represented.
Paris, London, Frankfurt and Brussels are some of the most important.
The agreement, for which no figures have yet been announced, is planned for five years.
On the other hand, Ferrovial, the Government of Castile-La Mancha and the University of Alcalá de Henares yesterday signed a protocol on cooperation to create an innovation centre for intelligent infrastructure.
The alliance is planning investments of 20 million by 2012, of which 50% will come from Ferrovial.
One of the tasks of the centre will be the study of energy efficiency at motorways and airports.
Acciona competes with Hochtief and Bouygues for its first motorway construction in Australia
Acciona is campaigning for the approval of its first highway in Australia, a market where they are already represented as energy and water companies.
The construction is a tunnel that will cost €1.7 billion (approximately €1.047 billion).
The French company Bouygues and the German Hochtief are its competitors.
A 5-kilometre-long tunnel in the Australian city of Brisbane, on the east coast, has become the best opportunity for Acciona to establish itself in the country as a construction company and highway operator.
The city administration wants to complete the construction at the end of 2014.
After the administration had opted for a public-private cooperation (PPP is the English abbreviation) to advance the project according to a business plan drawn up by Ernst & Young, the administration is already in possession of a definitive list of candidates for construction and toll management.
In anticipation of the offerings presented in May, the estimated investments amount to $1.7 billion (€1,047 billion), with three consortiums, consisting mainly of European construction companies competing with each other in the final phase.
The group called Transcity is led by Acciona, the only Spanish company, and its partners are BMD and Ghella.
The first company is one of Australia's largest construction companies, while the second, based in Italy, is one of the best specialists in civil engineering.
Acciona's Northern Direct consortium, formed by the British company Laing O'Rourke, Australia's Transfield, which is responsible for the infrastructures, and the French Bouygues assembly.
The third and final consortium, which is shortlisted, is called LBRJV, formed from the capital of the Australian Leighton (subsidiary of the German construction company Hochtief, which in turn belongs to ACS), the also native Baulderstone (owned by the German group Bilfinger Berger) and the French company Razel, which specializes in public construction.
The Australian market for infrastructures promises enormous construction work and privatizations, but has a hurdle to overcome, because you only get access through the purchase of a local construction company.
A strategy followed by these companies Hochtief or Bilfinger, in addition to Asian references, and which has yet to be pursued by the Spanish construction giants.
Even ACS has only gained access to this market through its participation of 30% in Hochtief, owner of the mentioned Leighton.
Milliors of assets
Acciona relies on this geographical area of the utmost importance for the industry, in which it is already very well-known because of its activity as an energy supplier and in the desalination industry.
Under other assets, it already has its largest windmill farm (192 MW) in Victoria and leads the group of companies tasked to build and manage the Adelaide desalination plant with a budget of $700 million.
His intention now is to consolidate in these two areas and use these synergies to gain access to the construction and infrastructure branches.
The underground toll route, promoted by the City of Brisbane's Office of Infrastructure and called Northern Link (northern feeders), has the purpose of linking the western highway in Toowong with the bypass in Kelvin Grove (see map) over a length of 5 kilometers through tunnels. This is the greatest measure to reduce congestion on the roads of Brisbane.
The timetable issued by the city administration envisages the awarging for summer 2010 and the start of construction work in December next year.
Even if this toll track is already to open to traffic in the last months of 2014, it is expected that the construction work will continue until 2016.
The tunnel was designed in 2005.
It has two lanes in each direction, an electronic toll system and a complex venting system.
The Queensland government is contributing 500 million Australian dollars (308 million euros) in the financing.
For Hochtief, Brisbane is already a big deal.
Australia is repeatedly awardinging substantial orders to Hochtief, which signed a 154 million contract with the government yesterday.
ACS, through its local subsidiary Leighton, will improve the infrastructure of the domestic broadband network with fiber optic cables.
This improvement will create fast internet access for 400,000 people and employ the German company for 18 months.
On the other hand, the company has received King George Tower's 27-storey construction project in the Australian city of Brisbane. Construction work has not yet begun and Hochtief has received 129 million for this.
Also in the United Kingdom, in Manchester it competes with Laing O'Rourke for the construction and management of two schools on 25 years.
The initial investment amounts to 75 million euros.
FCC awarded contract for a tunnel in Slovenia for 64 million
FCC has secured the construction of a €2.1-kilometre tunnel for a motorway in Slovenia through its subsidiary Alpine over the sum of €64.5 million.
The company received this contract only a few days after it was awarded the contract for the construction work to expand the Bosruck (Austria) tunnel over 130 million.
In this way, Alpine strengthens its experience in tunnel construction.
The start of the construction work is planned for the beginning of 2010 and its implementation will run over 32 months.
Sra. Rushmore receives advertising budget from Renfe
Renfe has attributed the advertising and marketing services to Sra. Rushmore agency for the next two years over a sum of approximately three million euros annually, the railway company announced.
In this contract there is also the possibility of two extensions of 12 months each. Sra. Rushmore was selected among 16 agencies that presented to this competition advertised by Renfe, 4 of which came into the final round, including TBWA, which has been responsible for advertising in the last three years.
From now on, Sra. Rushmore will be tasked with designing and manufacturing the campaigns.
Penalty over €63 million for France Télécom for slowing down the competition.
France's competition regulator in France has imposed a €63 million penalty for anti-competitive behaviour in the Caribian territories belonging to the country.
According to the authority, the telephone provider has restricted competition for landlines and mobile phones on the verge of regulation by signing exclusive contracts, pricing plans and loyalty programs for consumers.
Together with this sanction, the former French monopoly and still state-owned company has accumulated more than €560 million in fines since 1994 for obstructing its competitors.
The penalty imposed yesterday has even been increased as the authority, which monitors the competition, is of the opinion that France Télécom committed similar violations in the past and has therefore relapsed.
Application trading
On the other hand, the subsidiary of the French company has followed the example of other telephone providers and has opened an application trading site on the Internet for the purpose of increasing the revenue from transactions that do not originate from the telephone connection.
In principle, this application website of Orange is active in France and the United Kingdom.
You have to wait until 2010 until these sites will also be available to other countries, such as Spain.
The game at the Champions League has earned Madrid and Barça 476.4 million since the start.
The Champions League has become a source of income for the football clubs since its creation in 1992.
So much so that Real Madrid and Barcelona have since taken 476.4 million, earning them the third and fifth place of the football clubs that made the most money in the league.
The leader of this list is Manchester United.
The leader of this list is Manchester United.
Winning UEFA's Champions League doesn't just bring glory, it's also one of the main sources of revenue for the big clubs.
According to UEFA, the league has distributed up to €5,362.5 million to the 105 teams (of which 12 are Spanish) since its inception in the 1992/1993 season.
Real Madrid and the F.C. Barcelona have benefited from this distribution.
The white club ranks third in Europe, which has made the most money through its participation, and the only one to win the trophy three times alongside AC Milan.
The reigning Catalan champion and last winner of the former European Cup in 1992 ranks in fifth place.
The list is headed by Manchester United and Bayern Munich, two teams that also took the most money through their participation in the past Champoins League.
even though they lost to Barça.
On the other hand, Spain is only in third place of the countries that were able to raise money through the champions, although it has more titles than everyone else (five, as opposed to four to Italy, three at England and two at Germany).
Distribution
This obvious contradiction is explained by the complicated money-sharing procedure that UEFA is applying.
In this financial year, the organisation, whose chairmanship Michel Platini holds, is expecting revenue of 1,090 million through the Champions League.
Of this money, UEFA envisages 413.1 million for fixed payments: each of the 20 football clubs that took part in the qualifying preliminary round (among them the Atlético de Madrid) received 2.1 million.
In addition, those who fought for a participation received 3.8 million through their mere attendance, in addition to the 550,000 euros for every game they contested.
There is also a bonus for winning (800,000 euros) and for a draw (400,000 per team). The clubs that have advanced to the quarter-finals will each receive three million; the four who have advanced to the quarter-finals, 3.3 million.
The last four get 4 million each.
The winner earns 9 million, as opposed to the second, which receives 5.2 million.
For example, a football club receives at least 7.1 million and a maximum of 31.2 million in fixed revenues.
Barça, in turn, earned €2.5 million with his victory in the European Super Cup in August.
However, there are also the variable payments for which 337.8 million are earmarked.
This money is allocated proportionally to the value of every single television market.
The Spanish is one of the first and has 4 assigned places.
Last year’s master will receive 40% of the money allocated, 30% of the second, 20% the third-placer, and 10% for fourth place.
The other part will be distributed depending on the number of games they play at this year's edition.
Nueva Rumasa Offers $61 Million for 29.9% Interest in Sos
Nueva Rumasa yesterday leaked details of the purchase offer of shares, with which it intends to acquire a ceiling of between 25 and 29.9% of Sos's capital.
A percentage that does not force them to make a public tender (opa) due to the number of shares.
Specifically, Nueva Rumasa offers €1,5025 per share, which will be paid out for ten years and with an interest rate of 1% annually due to this shift.
Yesterday, the Sos shares closed at 1.85 euros, which is why Nueva Rumasa values the company 18% below the market value.
According to Nuevan Rumasa, the price of 1.50 euros reflects the real valuation of Sos.
The offer is associated with the appointment of eight of the 15 advisers.
The Jeréz Group gives shareholders a 15-day period to communicate their interest in the sale of their shares.
CNMV assured that it had not been informed of this offer, even though Ruiz Mateo's company reaffirmed that it had made contact with the authority.
At a conclusion, the deposit would amount to 611.7 million, while the value of Sos is 254.27 million.
In the meantime, Sos continues to reorganize its management.
In an attempt to remain on the verge of possible purchase offers and the judicial quarrels of its ex-managers, the Jesús and Jaime Salazar brothers have announced the appointment of María Luisa Jordá as the head of internal accounting.
A decision that makes her the first woman to hold a high position at the food company.
This is a newly created item, which is directly undering the chairman of the group.
This is anything but polemic, because the company is engaged in a judicial battle on suspicion of reflecting more than 230 million from Sos to other societies of the Salazar family.
It cannot be ruled out that Sos will postpone further capital over the course of the next few months.
With regard to the Salazar's loan, ex-advisers Ildefonso Ortega and Ángel Fernández Noriega (CCM and Unicaja representatives) appeared before the National Assembly yesterday, confirming that they had approved the postponement of 212 million without knowing their destination.
CNMV Approves Paternina's Public Exclusion Tender Submitted by Investment Company Mer
The National Stock Exchange Commission (CNMV) approved the public exclusion tender for Federico Paternina submitted by the investment company Mer last October 9.
The supervisory authority stated that it approved this invitation to tender after it has been demonstrated that that the conditions comply with the legally binding laws and that the content of the submitted explanatory document can be considered "sufficient" following the amendments of last December 2.
CNMV has also noted that this offer is aimed at the acquisition of 550,008 shares of Federico Paternina at a price of €7.65 per share, which in turn represents 8.95% of the share capital consisting of €6,142,786 in shares admitted on the Madrid and Bilbao exchanges.
In addition, it has also been announced that 5,592,778 million shares have been permanently invested, which cannot be transferred in any way until the conclusion of the tender and whose price has been determined by Federico Paternina in accordance with the legally binding laws.
New programs for the assessment of vehicles
In these days of storms and accidents not only the motor vehicle workshops deserve
Thousands of vehicles involved in an accident are towed every day into the workshops, where an appraiser has to assess the damage incurred and the cost of repair.
Not a single accident is the same and the calculation of the costs for the parts and working hours can be a lengthy and complicated task.
Calculation of the repair costs of between 20,000 and 30,000 euros by hand, including the parts and working hours, can take up to two or three hours.
On the other hand, with the support of the latest IT tools, it is a matter of minutes
That’s whay, almost 100% of reviewers use these types of systems.
Service and application providers for the assessment of accidents and repair collect the information they receive from the manufacturers in order to process them afterwards and offer them to their customers in the form of a useful programme.
In Spain Audatex, part of Solera, is the market leader; 80% of all expert opinions are prepared with their products.
The other two companies that compete in the tool market for review and elaborating a report are GtMotive and Eurotax.
Working with the data that the manufacturers provide is anything but easy.
According to Eduardo Velázquez, sales manager of Audatex, it works with 63 manufacturers and importers, with each of them providing the information in a different format.
In addition, the amount of data to be processed is getting bigger and larger to the point that even more versions, variants and motorizations have been launched in the last five years than in the entire fifteen years.
As soon as a new car hits the market, work begins for the companies.
It is a tedious task, because every single one of the thousands of vehicle parts must be catagolized and its price entered.
In addition, an "intelligent" graphic image is created of each model, on which you can "click on" different parts of the vehicle.
If this is a much-sold model, the work can be completed in a week if the procedure proceeds swiftly.
If this is a less common car, it can take up to three or four months, with 99.2% of the cars marketed in Spain with complete information.
Among the more exclusive models, for example, they have information about the Porsche models, but no Ferrari or Lamborghini.
In view of the vehicle fleet travelling on the road, it is over 99%.
In order to carry out the documentation work and the manufacture of databases, Audatex has eighth centers (Spain, France, Germany, the USA, Brazil, Mexico, China and Japan) and each of them specializes in certain brands.
The national headquarters are located in Alcobendas (Madrid).
There, more than a hundred technicians (usually mechanical professionals) work simultaneously with three computer screens.
Audatex invests €90 million annually in the preparation of these databases.
Every month, they record 2.5 million dates and their customers get the updates every other day.
Elaborating this enormous flow of information enables companies to use them in various ways and thereby offer different products.
The most common use is the use for the repairs and repairs, however, depending on the country, there are also tools for the management of scrap parts or for calculating the file or residual value of a car.
The only company that informs about the value of used cars in Spain is Eurotax.
Audatex does not offer this offer in Spain, but in the United States.
It is easy to get an overview of the kind of support it gives to industry experts when reviewing the products that Audatex offers.
This company offers ten different tools, whereby the star of the products is AudaPlus, a standard solution for assessing accidents for the assessors.
It includes vehicles, motorcycles as well as light and heavy industrial vehicles.
In addition to the cost of the parts, it includes the repair times estimated by the manufacturer or painting prices.
This tool is paid for depending on the purpose, i.e. for each report.
It will be most expensive for customers, who rarely use it, a maximum of ten times a month, namely 5.75 euros per month.
On the other hand, every insurance company that prepares thousands of expert reports negotiates the price with Audatex.
With other products, such as AudaVIN, you can fully identify a vehicle and the equipment with which it ran off the assembly line based solely on the chassis number.
AudaGlass deals with vehicle windows, and AudaSubastas is an open service on the market on the Internet, which can be used for vehicles that have been declared a total loss.
Your statistical service is very useful in identifying trends, conducting geodemographic analyses, or for obtaining information about deviations by brand and model.
For example, it is possible to investigate how many models of a particular car brand had to go to the workshop due to breaks due to breakdowns or how many of them were involved in a serious accident during a certain period.
Gt Motive is the only Spanish company dedicated to the development of this type of computer tools.
Among other things, it distributes Gt Estimate, which is also intended for appraisers and supplies digital images in the same way, access to parts or prices and official working hours of the manufacturer.
Gt Motive is a company of the Einsa Group, which was founded in 1971 as a provider of services and solutions for the assessment of damage, breakdowns or maintenance of vehicles.
The GT leader for expert opinions is a reference product on the market.
They work with 24,000 users in workshops, 3,100 reviewers and 53 insurance companies.
Its business volume has risen at 20% annually over the last three years and sales amounted to €10.8 million in 2008.
At the beginning of last year, they also began to go to the international market with the opening of an office in Paris.
Audatex, on the other hand, was founded in Germany in 1966 and established in Spain in 1979.
According to the company's sources, 62% of its business is done in Europe and the rest of the world, and the remaining 38% in North and South America. They work with 900 insurance companies and 33,000 workshops, 3,000 of them in Spain.
Total sales in the Solera world (Audatex, Sidexa, Informex ABZ, Hollander and IMS) is $557 million, 3.35 more than in 2008.
In this country, the company has revenues of 19.1 million euros, 7.2% more than in the previous year.
In 2005, the Solera group was worth $1 billion on the stock exchange and today its shares are traded at $2.4 billion.
They have been part of the New York Stock Exchange since 2007 and part of the Standard & Poor's benchmark index.
Auction of Accident Cars on the Internet
Last October, the Solera Autoonline group bought a platform on the Internet for the sale of accident vehicles and motorcycles.
This purchase meant the payment of €59.5 million for 85% of the company's capital, which could increase to the remaining 15% next year.
The purpose of this purchase was to offer its customers more services and value enhancement, with the possibility of gaining access to a huge international market.
This review and purchase service is aimed exclusively at industry professionals, such as insurance companies, appraisers, car rental companies, workshops, junkyards and car dealers, who must register before their activities.
This platform was founded in Germany in 1996 and manages more than 650,000 operations throughout Europe, 500,000 of them in Germany alone.
Its main markets are Spain, Greece, Poland and Turkey.
The site nowadays has more than 1,500 registered sellers and 4,000 reviewers.
Every day, 3,000 ads are managed and 100 new ads are added every day on the Spanish market.
According to the Spanish legislation, a vehicle whose chassis number has been deregistered may no longer drive on the roads, but certain non-damaged parts may be used as spare parts.
On the other hand, cars with historical value may be allowed again, even if they have been deregistered after difficult administrative procedures.
Cost estimate of the workshop in four steps
With the Auda-Taller tool, Audatex ensures that the user receives a cost estimate in just four steps:identification of the vehicle, search of the spare part, creation and preparation of a cost estimate.
The easy handling of these systems is a fundamental condition, especially to convince the older professionals, who are usually more or less opposed to the use of these new computer techniques.
The database includes 1,034 vehicles, 666 of which are passenger vehicles, 109 SUVs, 137 motorcycles, 78 vans and 44 trucks.
Of course you need a computer with an internet connection for use.
After the model to be repaired has been identified on the basis of the chassis number, a graphic of the respective model appears and after that the required spare part is selected.
The user can include variables, such as the price for the working hours, surcharges or discounts and after that he can have the cost estimate printed out and passed on to his customer.
AudaTaller, however, is not a tool for assessment like AudaPlus, but rather a reference catalogue.
The main difference between the two systems is that which is focused on the workshop does not involve estimated working hours.
The usage costs for this tool are 350 euros per year, an amount that the customer can easily pay.
Currently, the company Audatex is working to be able to offer these images in three-dimensional format.
This is an innovation that car mechanics have been waiting for for a long time, because you can choose a door with it, for example, and you can then turn the picture over completely to look at the inside.
